#: Package: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid "Pretty printing for well-behaved Show instances"
msgstr "Snygg utskrift för väluppförda Show-instanser"

#. Summary
#: Package: libghc-groom-doc
msgid "Pretty printing for well-behaved Show instances; documentation"
msgstr "Snygg utskrift för väluppförda Show-instanser; dokumentation"

#. Summary
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof
msgid "Pretty printing for well-behaved Show instances; profiling libraries"
msgstr "Snygg utskrift för väluppförda Show-instanser; profileringsbibliotek"

#. Description
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof Package: libghc-groom-doc Package:
#: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid ""
"Automatically derived Show instances are an easy way to inspect data in your"
" program.  However, for large data-structures, the resulting output lacks "
"whitespace, making it unreadable.  Groom offers an replacement to `show' "
"called `groom' which attempts to pretty-print the output of `show'.  For "
"example:"
msgstr ""
"Automatiskt härledda Show-instanser är ett enkelt sätt att granska data i "
"ditt program. För stora datastrukturer saknar den resulterande utdata dock "
"blanksteg, vilket gör den oläslig. Groom erbjuder en ersättning för `show’ "
"med namnet `groom’ som försöker snyggformatera utdatan från `show’. Till "
"exempel:"

#. Description
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof Package: libghc-groom-doc Package:
#: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid ""
"> let x = parseExp \"foobar 1 [1,2]\" > in do >   putStrLn (show x) >   "
"putStrLn (groom x)"
msgstr ""
"> let x = parseExp \"foobar 1 [1,2]\" > in do >   putStrLn (show x) >   "
"putStrLn (groom x)"

#. Description
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof Package: libghc-groom-doc Package:
#: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid "results in:"
msgstr "resulterar i:"

#. Description
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof Package: libghc-groom-doc Package:
#: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid ""
"> ParseOk (App (App (Var (UnQual (Ident \"foobar\"))) (Lit (Int 1))) (List "
"[Lit (Int 1),Lit (Int 2)])) > ParseOk >   (App (App (Var (UnQual (Ident "
"\"foobar\"))) (Lit (Int 1))) >      (List [Lit (Int 1), Lit (Int 2)]))"
msgstr ""
"> ParseOk (App (App (Var (UnQual (Ident \"foobar\"))) (Lit (Int 1))) (List "
"[Lit (Int 1),Lit (Int 2)])) > ParseOk >   (App (App (Var (UnQual (Ident "
"\"foobar\"))) (Lit (Int 1))) >      (List [Lit (Int 1), Lit (Int 2)]))"

#. Description
#: Package: libghc-groom-prof Package: libghc-groom-doc Package:
#: libghc-groom-dev Package: haskell-groom-utils
msgid ""
"Groom works only on Show instances that output valid Haskell code; if Groom "
"can't understand its input, it will not make any changes."
msgstr ""
"Groom fungerar endast på Show-instanser som matar ut giltig Haskell-kod; om "
"Groom inte kan förstå sina indata gör det inga ändringar."

#. Summary
#: Package: libghc-happy-lib-dev Package: haskell-happy-lib-data
msgid "parser generator for Haskell"
msgstr "tolkgenerator för Haskell"

#. Summary
#: Package: libghc-happy-lib-doc
msgid "parser generator for Haskell; documentation"
msgstr "tolkgenerator för Haskell; dokumentation"

#. Summary
